      "description": "The Kannawa district is the spiritual heart of Beppu's onsen culture, where plumes of steam rise from every alleyway. Visitors can cook eggs and vegetables in the natural steam vents (jigoku-mushi), soak in dozens of local bathhouses, and experience the enigmatic 'Steam Bathing' tradition.",
